message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal but complete example of an **interactive rotating card** that flips around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy/paste this into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Global styles ----------
   (optional – just to center the card) */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- Card container ----------
   Sets up 3D context & perspective */
.card-wrapper {
    width:300px;          /* card width */
    height:200px;         /* card height */
    perspective:800px;    /* depth perception */
}

/* ---------- Card itself ----------
   Uses backface-visibility to hide the backside during rotation */
.card {
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    position:relative;
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* enable 3D transforms on children */
    transition:transform .6s ease;    /* smooth animation */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- Front face ----------
   Positioned absolutely so it sits on top of the back face */
.front, .back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide when facing away */
    border-radius:10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

/* ---------- Front styling ----------
   Normal view */
.front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.front h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.5rem;
}
.front p {
    margin:0;
    color:#555;
}

/* ---------- Back styling ----------
   Rotated 180° so it's hidden initially */
.back {
    background:#333;
    color:#fff;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* start flipped */
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-size:1.2rem;
}

/* ---------- Hover effect ----------
   Flip the whole card on hover */
.card:hover {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <h2>Front Side</h2>
            <p>This is the front of the card.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            Backside content goes here!
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective:800px`). |
| `.card` | Holds both faces; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows child elements to maintain their 3D positions. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each occupies the same space; `backface-visibility:hidden` hides the side that's turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° so it’s hidden. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the entire card 180°, revealing the back face. |

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or add more content inside each face. Happy coding!
